{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits","id":856576,"title":"Sample spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-31T10:31:52-07:00","id":856576,"title":"Sample spirits","content":"Is there a thread or a corner of the forum with sample spirits for 2nd edition? Or a place to crowd-test new spirits as it were?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T12:42:53-07:00","id":856657,"title":"","content":"Just post them here and we will pass them through the Gauntlet! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T16:53:23-07:00","id":856776,"title":"","content":"Here a batch of more &quot;Generic&quot; spirits that I have used in game.a few use Numina that haven't re-appeared in 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Blood Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2 (Spirit)<br /> Power 4, Finesse 6, Resistance 4, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>7<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Blood 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only manifest where blood has recently been spilled<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Styptic Herbs<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Desiccate, Drain, Heal, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b>Darkness Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 11<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Darkness 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot remain in the presence of bright light<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Fire<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Fetter, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Concealment, Innocuous<br /> <br /> <b>Disease Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> Power 7, Finesse 7, Resistance 6, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 13<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 19<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Disease 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Dematerialize in the presence of a Healer<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Medicinal Plants<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Blast, Drain, Hallucination, Innocuous, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <b>Knowledge Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Knowledge 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must acquire new information<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Remains of destroyed information<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Innocuous, Omen Trance, Telekinesis, Telepathy<br /> <br /> <b>Murder Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 7, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 14<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus</b>: 7<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Death 2, Violence 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot enter consecrated ground<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Bones of an executed murderer<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Dement, Hallucination, Phantom Arsenal, Rapture, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <b>Rage Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> Power 7, Finesse 3, Resistance 4, Willpower 7, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Anger 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest in the presence of fresh lavender<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Lavender petals<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Emotional Aura, Speed, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Storm Spirit </b><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> Power 10, Finesse 8, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 18<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 10<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 25<br /> <b>Size:</b> 7<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 17<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Storm 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest or use influence on a clear day.<br /> <b>Bane:</b> People and items that have survived a lighting strike.<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Concealment, Elemental Immunity (Lightning), Phantom Arsenal, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Stalwart, Wail<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T11:36:10-07:00","id":858420,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Thrice-Veiled</b></span><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 9, Finesse 12, Resistance 9<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 25<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 21<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 23<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 15<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Secrets \u2022\u2022, Harmony \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Image, Reaching, Shadow Gateway<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Implant Mission, Innocuous, Seek, Sign<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Anyone who presents the spirit with a piece of Theban limestone inscribed with a simple &quot;fact,&quot; the Thrice-Veiled will use its power to make the fact come true. For example, the words &quot;Mike Jones is a wealthy homeowner&quot; on such a stone will mean the spirit bends its power to contrive a certain homeless man' ascendance to the upper class. <br /> <b>Bane:</b> ******[NOT SURE ABOUT THIS ONE YET]<br /> <b>Description: </b>The Thrice-Veiled appears as an indistinct figure -- blurred, dark, and even when you see him, you can never remember what he looks like.<br /> <br /> The Thrice-Veiled is a powerful servitor of the God Amun. The Thrice-Veiled deals in secrets (everything from where the bodies are to the Bans of half the local spirit court), but it is primarily involved with harmony. In this context, harmony can mean the proper functioning of the body, the local infrastructure, or society. Everyone plays their parts; even criminals have their place, but everyone knows their place and the spirit discourages imbalance and undue frictions. For example, when a mugger confronts his victim, the victim will put up little resistance and the mugger will take the money and go. Likewise, when the mugger is cornered by the police, he will surrender and the cop will not use undue force. The &quot;order&quot; which this <i>Ensah</i> gradually imposes on a locale isn't necessarily congruent with the &quot;good&quot; -- there is still destitution, crime, and inequality. But when the Thrice-Veiled is watching, the locals are, if not content, then a little less discontented with their lot. Of course, someone looking to shake up the status quo -- a gang, activists, or a pack of Uratha -- may find themselves facing pushback from the Shadows.<br /> <br /> Summoned by Neferankhet the leader of the local mystery cult, The Thrice-Veiled is the strongest spirit of the temple complex, and acts as an avatar of Amun. It helps to hide the temple and the worshippers. It also helps to keep order in the general area -- people tend not to litter, buildings and vehicles are kept up, and crime is kept to a petty level. The spirit acknowledges the authority of Neferankhet. In turn, it gains much essence from the worshippers and the locus, and is setting about to change the spiritual landscape in the neighborhood. As befits the &quot;behind the scenes&quot; style of the spirit, the local spirit courts are slow to realize there is a cunning new player in town.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T12:53:23-07:00","id":858462,"title":"","content":"The Bane could be a perfectly balanced blade, as evidenced by an Armor Piercing rating of 4 or above. Or reflective glass: It must appear as it is before it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:21:11-07:00","id":861127,"title":"","content":"Here a few more individual Spirits<br /> <hr /><br /> <b>Bright Cursor</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bright Cursor is a helpful (if somewhat alien) spirit that draws essence from computerized devices, such as smart phones or laptops. Bright Cursor appears to be a blinking ball of light surrounded by a cloud of phantom text, images and sounds. It uses its influence to ensure optimum performance<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 6, Resistance 3, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 5, <b>Size</b> 2, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 5, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Communication Devices 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Goes into hibernation if covered in crushed glass; Bane<b><i>:</i> </b>Fulgurite/Petrified Lightning<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Blast (Electricity), Host Jump, Left Handed Spanner, Sign</span> <hr /><br /> <b>The Chains of Vice</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Chains of Vice is a spirit of death and addiction. Its draws is power from lives lost to excessive indulgence in vice. The entity can take human form, and appears as a tall man, with pale skin, thinning hair, and dressed in a black suit and pork pie hat. In its true form, The Chains of Vice appears as an inhumanly tall and lanky creature, with chalk white skin and no discernable facial features or gender. Its wrists and ankles are bound by chains of brass.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 7, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Addiction 1, Death 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person that has fasted for 3days; <b>Bane:</b> Ashes of an Addict<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Implant Mission, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Rapture, Seek</span> <hr /><br /> <b>Dreaming Kweo</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Spirit named \u201cDreaming Kweo\u201d protects the dreams of those that dwell within its territories. It hunts any creature that preys upon dreams, and can travel between the Shadow and Dream Space of a sleeper with ease. When manifested, Dreaming Kweo is a sleek, muscular Mexican gray wolf roughly the size of a horse. His fur is dark as the evening sky, traced with patterns similar to the weave of a dreamcatcher and his eyes, teeth, and claws glow with starlight.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 29<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Dreams 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot withdraw from battle until the enemy retreats or is defeated; <b>Bane: </b>Cottonwood<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Dreamwalker*, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Shattering Howl), Essence Thief, Regenerate, Seek, Speed<br /> <br /> <i><b>Manifestation - Dreamwalker:</b> (Requires Open Condition) by spending 2 Essence, the entity shifts from Twilight into the Dream Space of an individual or location with the Open condition. Once there, it can interact with the Dream Space in the same way it interacts with the real world (including other entities also active in the Dream Space), and may use influence and numina.</i></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T12:18:17-07:00","id":861201,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> You are a treasure to the forum good-being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T13:40:38-07:00","id":861260,"title":"","content":"Something a little different, but I've made an STL and 3D prints for the lock spirits in Dark Eras. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.thingiverse.com/thing:1400733\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.thingiverse.com/thing:1400733</a><br /> <br /> I'll give making a couple of these a shot too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T16:15:43-07:00","id":862253,"title":"","content":"some more spirits <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Forgotten Pain</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Forgotten Pain is a spirit that feeds on the apathy that some caregivers in hospices and nursing homes develop over time. It uses it powers to manifest as a non-descript middle aged woman dressed in the clothing of a nurse or orderly. Its true form is of an androgynous living statue of ivory. It has a crown of obsidian horns, six arms, and dark eyes that weep black tears.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Apathy 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person wearing Witch Hazel flowers; <b>Bane:</b> Witch Hazel<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Drain, Emotional Aura (Apathy), Mortal Mask, Stalwart, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mother Chrysalis</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Mother Chrysalis an ancient spirit of metamorphosis that uses its power to physically and spiritually transform those who make the proper offerings and sacrifices to her. The entity appears as a massive black moth with glowing eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 10, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 30<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Metamorphosis 4<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use influence on an unwilling subject; <b>Bane:</b> Powdered moth chrysalis<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Fetter, Image, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Drain, Essence Thief, Heal*, Metamorphosis*, Omen Trance, Regenerate, Telekinesis</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina - Heal: </b>The entity can heal others\u2019 wounds, typically for a hefty price. This Numen costs 1 Essence and a Power+ Finesse roll to activate. Each success heals a level of bashing damage, while two successes can heal a point of lethal damage. The lethal damage healed can be used to mend aggravated damage, but each point of aggravated damage cured costs three additional points of Essence. This power may also be used to fight off disease or the effects of poison \u2014 each success adding to the subjects\u2019 resistance rolls on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina- Metamorphosis: </b>When working on an incapacitated or unresisting living creature, the entity can alter that creature\u2019s physical make up. This Numen requires a Finesse + Resistance roll to activate. Changes such as the targets appearance, race, or gender cost 3 Essence. Other, more substantial, changes may also be made. By spending 5 Essence, the entity can move one Attribute dot or turn an Attribute dot into one of:<br /> \u2022 A point of Armor<br /> \u2022 1L of natural weaponry rating<br /> \u2022 A sense that the victim does not normally possess (such as echolocation, infrared vision, or similar)<br /> \u2022 A Dread Power that suits the change in question</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The One Who Burns</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The One Who Burns is a spirit of fire and reckless aggression. It uses it influence to trigger arson and violent outbursts; feeding from the resulting chaos and destruction. The One who Burns takes the form of a vaguely female creature of impressive stature. Its body is cracked and blackened as if by flame and noxious smoke rises from its form. Boiling hot blood seeps from its blistered flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 7, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 13, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fire 2, Violence 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot harm a true pacifist; <b>Bane:</b> Holly (a plant representing peaceful accord)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Posses, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Aggressive Meme, Blast (Fire), Emotional Aura (Anger), Firestarter, Regenerate, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Prince of Hungers</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Prince of Hungers is a spirit of gluttony and conspicuous consumption. It is often summoned by individuals seeking material gain, especially when the resources are used to support other appetites. When manifested, The Prince of Hungers is a corpulent 10ft tall giant, whose bald head is absent any features except for its oversized mouth with an impossible number of teeth. It always appears in clothing that would consider \u201cfinery\u201d, which could be anything from an expensive suit to opulent robes, all cut to flatter his girth.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Gluttony 2, Wealth 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must consume any edible item presented on a golden platter <b>Bane: </b>Azalea Blossoms<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Drain, Rapture, Stalwart, Telekinesis, Transmute</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T18:52:21-07:00","id":862343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=861201#post861201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> You are a treasure to the forum good-being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. These are awesome!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.thingiverse.com/thing:1477319\" target=\"_blank\">Here's my take on the Bright Cursor</a>, although I diverged a bit from the description based off of the resources I could find. I think it sticks with the spirit (ha!) of the description. I've also got some photos of my trial print: <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://orig01.deviantart.net/176d/f/2016/099/4/f/cursor_spirit_1_by_peace__out-d9yc6as.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://orig10.deviantart.net/497d/f/2016/099/b/0/cursor_spirit_2_by_peace__out-d9yc6gf.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The pictures don't quite do it justice, I'm actually quite fond of it. I'll work on taking a crack at a couple of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T15:32:04-07:00","id":862805,"title":"","content":"Excellent. Please continue!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T08:19:59-07:00","id":863159,"title":"","content":"A few more for today -<br /> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Ragged Tear</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Ragged Tear is a pain spirt that feeds on deliberate cruelty, and uses its influence to compel individuals to greater acts of emotional and physical sadism. It manifests as a dark-skinned, hairless and androgynous person, with empty eye sockets that leak a black fluid and is dressed in tattered wrappings of dark fabric.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2 [Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Cruelty 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Is repelled by the \u201cAko Konan\u201d, a symbol of West African origin, associated with mercy <b>Bane: </b>Frankincense Resin<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Seek</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Screaming Void</b></span><br /> The Screaming Void is a strange spirit from the darker reaches of the Shadow, drawing its power from entropy and dissolution. It appears as a rippling distortion in the air accompanied by a high-pitched resonant noise.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 3, <b>Initiative</b> 18, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 30<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Entropy 3, Sound 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only manifest in locations with a great amount of decay and neglect; <b>Bane:</b> A weapon plated in platinum<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Dement, Entropic Decay, Essence Thief, Left-Handed Spanner, Seek, Speed, Stalwart</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Storm of Dread</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Spirit called Strom of Dread regains essence when creatures die from electrocution. It formed most of its identity from the execution of death row inmates via the electric chair. Since this form of execution is no longer common, Storm of Dread must seek its essence in other ways. Storm of Dread takes the form of a cloud of black smoke, crackling with lighting and carrying the lingering smells of ozone and burning flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 7, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Electricity 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Loses Essence if submerged in salt water; <b>Bane:</b> Wood struck by lightning<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Claim, Fetter, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Blast (Lightning), Host Jump, Left-Handed Spanner, Regenerate, Speed, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Unyielding Lord</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Unyielding Lord is a spirit of Vengeance, especially acts of vengeance taken to satisfy ones pride. It uses it power to inflame petty insults and minor grievances to a violent extreme. It uses possession frequently, and prefers to occupy the bodies of wealthy professionals. The Unyielding Lord appears as a powerfully muscled red-skinned man, with two heads (each a fierce lion), the wings of an eagle, and writhing swarms of scarabs for arms.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Vengeance 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must always keep its Word; <b>Bane:</b> Lily of the Valley (a flower representing humility)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Claim, Fetter, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Implant Mission, Pierce Mind, Regenerate, Seek, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Whisper in the Hall</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Whisper in the Hall is a spirit dwells within schools, and derives its essence from the dedication and pride the students and faculty have for that institution. While normally harmless, it has begun to use its influence to encourage ever greater demonstrations of loyalty and to punish those who do not show the proper amount of \u201cschool spirit\u201d. It appears as a vaguely humanoid swirl of posters, banners and bulletins from the school. It often manifests as a quiet, non-descript student, dressed in the school colors.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Pride 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only influence Faculty, Students or Alumni;<b> Bane: </b>A class ring from a rival school<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Rapture</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T10:08:37-07:00","id":892596,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for a spirit of justice by opression.<br /> Or police justice spirits?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T19:06:34-07:00","id":892938,"title":"","content":"try this - <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tarnished Badge</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cTarnished Badge\u201d is a spirit that draws its strength from the abuse of the authority granted to police officers and others who enforce the law. The uses its power to urge law officers down the path of corruption. Tarnished Badge appears as a broad shouldered man wearing an antiquated policeman\u2019s uniform. Its face is smooth and featureless except for its eyes, which flash with red light.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 17<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Authority 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot physically harm a law officer unless attacked first; <b>Bane:</b> bones of a person unjustly slain by police<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Revolver), Host Jump, Regenerate, Seek</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T07:03:14-07:00","id":893270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=892938#post892938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">try this - <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tarnished Badge</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cTarnished Badge\u201d is a spirit that draws its strength from the abuse of the authority granted to police officers and others who enforce the law. The uses its power to urge law officers down the path of corruption. Tarnished Badge appears as a broad shouldered man wearing an antiquated policeman\u2019s uniform. Its face is smooth and featureless except for its eyes, which flash with red light.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 17<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Authority 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot physically harm a law officer unless attacked first; <b>Bane:</b> bones of a person unjustly slain by police<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Revolver), Host Jump, Regenerate, Seek</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks! Sometimes is quite hard to imagine certain things.<br /> My game is about a pack working as a fight club that time to time go to missions around the neighborhood doing justice by their own hands first discovering a crime, punishing and then calling police leaving the criminal. <br /> <br /> The pack territory is a mess of crime, poverty, drugdealers, but still is a neighborhood with normal and good people living around.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a long season in the Shadow with all these details because I'm actualy afraid of so much information and my brain cant figure it out what is the appearence of all of this in buildings etc. I dont want to fill the spiritual streets with spirits clones of each other too.<br /> Any tips discribing the basic Shadow version of this territory?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T16:58:34-07:00","id":893734,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Shadow of the Streets</b><br /> <br /> I would not be able to give anything close to a &quot;universal&quot; shadow landscape for a rough neighborhood, every storyteller is going to approach it differently. But I can share how I approach it.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is a place written in symbol, metaphor, and analogy; where emotions and events are given shape and exaggerated to a monstrous degree. So lets look at the elements<br /> <br /> <b>Crime - </b>The Alleyways where people are mugged and robbed become long corridors with high walls; claustrophobic and giving the impression of being followed. broken teeth crunch underfoot.<br /> The hideout of the gangs that run the neighborhood become graffiti fortresses, their colors and signs becoming pennants that blow in a spectral wind.<br /> The expensive cars of the pimps become predatory spirits; loud, gaudy, leaving a scent of sex and desperation in its exhaust.<br /> The places where bodies are dumped seep with clotting blood, while shapes wrapped in plastic and bound with rope jut upwards like tombstones.<br /> <br /> <b>Poverty - </b>Despite recent attempts at gentrification, the Shadow remembers all the small businesses that have come and gone in the cheep strip mall, each doorway and window crowds into the next like crooked teeth. A stale breeze carries an impression of defeat and frustrated ambition.<br /> The phantom homes resemble shantytowns - ramshackle and run down, with dark bars on every window that serve to trap the dreams and desires of its residents.<br /> The spirits shuffle aimlessly, they take the form of caricatures of the homeless , made of discarded rubbish tattered cloths.<br /> <br /> <b>Drugs - </b>The Drug Dens are places decaying from the inside out, spirits of addiction and pleasure commingle. A thick smoke that dulls the senses billow from the open windows and the grass on the lawn is interspersed with broken vials and discarded needles.The spirits whisper sweet encouragements, to take another hit, just this once.<br /> <br /> <b>The Good Folk</b> - There are places in this dark landscape that resonate with other emotions. There are homes that shine with a warm light. There are are entire blocks that radiate ambition, pride, and diligence. There are parks that echo with laughter and music; that carry the scent of a cook out and that no dark spirit dares to enter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T19:14:25-07:00","id":893795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=893270#post893270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks! Sometimes is quite hard to imagine certain things.<br /> My game is about a pack working as a fight club that time to time go to missions around the neighborhood doing justice by their own hands first discovering a crime, punishing and then calling police leaving the criminal.<br /> <br /> The pack territory is a mess of crime, poverty, drugdealers, but still is a neighborhood with normal and good people living around.<br /> <br /> I haven't done a long season in the Shadow with all these details because I'm actualy afraid of so much information and my brain cant figure it out what is the appearence of all of this in buildings etc. I dont want to fill the spiritual streets with spirits clones of each other too.<br /> Any tips discribing the basic Shadow version of this territory?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to make it about a high population of clone spirits, you can make it about a very powerful Drug/Crime Spirit that rules a brood of lesses individuals, wich then are very similar. A king with knights. The knights might look like each other at first glance, specially the very weak ones, but the King is always there, and can come to aid the knights at every moment. There might be a clash between two broods, the Crime/Drug brood and nature spirits that are still present. A river spirit could be fighting to keep its resonance pure by getting rid of the bodies that are dumped on it, while drug/crime spirits are trying to destroy the older spirits to get a clean territory to feed and grow.<br /> <br /> Edit: Or you can just read Reighnhell's post and ignore mine... Hahahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":".  Edited after Reighnhell's awesomeness... 05-18-2016, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T22:25:22-07:00","id":893858,"title":"","content":"I used some house rules for the derive traits. If anyone has suggestions for alternate Bans, Banes, Numina or any other trait, please tell me.<br /> <br /> <b>Golden Heights</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Born from the ruthless ambition and paranoia that permeates corporate environments, this spirit is not only powerful and subtle, it is personal. It loves to use its powers to pose as workers of different ranks, pulling strings here and there and nursing the Essence of intrigue like a fine Cuban cigar.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> When posing as a mortal of high status, it is usually male, and always over 7 feet tall and charming regardless of weight. Its blonde hair and beard are finely groomed, its smile is a lighthouse and all its clothes and accessories are much better than yours. When posing as one of low status, it looks normal for its surroundings and is easily overlooked. It is often followed and helped by lesser spirits of bureaucracy, procrastination, greed, envy and similar concepts. In its true form, Golden Heights is a humanoid mass of different masks that quietly laugh, curse and lick their lips. Behind each mask are human eyes whose optic nerves can stretch and bend around corners. Its putrefied hands are always busy making gestures of confidence and masterful planning.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> It delights in lending its Numina through Grant Blessing, no matter if the target is an errand boy or a Sponsored. Occasionally, when it sees an especially promising worker, it will tell them about the supernatural players hiding in certain corporations. Most of the mortals who delve too deep into this end up fired under dubious circumstances or disappear, but a few manage to please a supernatural faction enough to join it and become &quot;one of them&quot; (usually a ghoul, wolf-blooded and such).</span><br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 10, Finesse 10, Resistance 8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Maximum Essence/Per Turn:</b> 40/12<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 14<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 14<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Intrigue \u2022\u2022\u2022, Ambition \u2022\u2022\u2022<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Fetter, Materialize, Discorporate, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578026-new-spirit-manifestation-sponsorship\"><b>Sponsorship</b></a><br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/626202-new-numina\"><b>Grant Blessing</b></a>, Hallucination, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/626202-new-numina\"><b>Sever Fetter</b></a>, Sign, Mortal Mask, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/824054-2e-conversion-numina\"><b>Price Of Power</b></a> x 1 (Eye Spy)<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 1:</b> Cannot abide the presence of someone with the Virtue of Charity, Honesty, Loyalty or Diligence (or equivalent words).<br /> <br /> <b>Ban 2: </b>Must use its powers to apply Notoriety or Leveraged to a rival if the requester claims someone else's work as their own.<br /> <br /> <b>Bane:</b> A symbol or badge of high corporate status (assume 3 or 4 dots) acquired without committing a single crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 05-19-2016, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T06:01:09-07:00","id":893967,"title":"","content":"My god I wish I had this imagination. GMing Werewolf has been a real strange and hard experience because I used to GM Mage and Changeling and both of those games has strange &quot;worlds&quot; linked to then looking more difficult to imagine, but they are still personal in the way that these strange worlds are not dependent on humanity vice versa, you just imagine crazy stuff that fits better for your main story and voil\u00e1. but Werewolf you really need to create two detailed worlds focusing on your territory. And even more, assuming that the characters start with a pack, totem and everything the campaign will always require at least a minimum level of description that Reighnhell has given me.<br /> <br /> I rly thank <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\">Reighnhell</a></b> for that wonderful description. That give me some ideas to start mapping the territory.<br /> <br /> And thanks to <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly\">BinAly</a></b> because its pretty hard to assume that the spiritual realm is all about diversity without making a complete chaos or turning everything to generic.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","user":"magisanctum","date":". 05-28-2016, 07:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T04:24:05-07:00","id":896016,"title":"","content":"There is some really great stuff here! If you're still taking inspirations / requests, Reign, I've got a river spirit in my game that needs fleshing out... <br /> <br /> It is a river spirit - who I've been picturing as a giant, half-glimpsed water snake - which local Uratha have occasionally bargained with to bring them across the Gauntlet with its Abduct numen. However, the hidden spring that feeds the river has been tainted by Pure rites, and the spirit is growing increasingly violent, frenzied and bloodthirsty. It has secretly been attempting to lure people into the water from a bridge just out of town.<br /> <br /> I'm a little stumped about Bans and Banes, though. I don't know whether it can be &quot;un-tainted&quot;, but I'd love ideas about what it could have been like both before and after its change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T08:04:03-07:00","id":896085,"title":"","content":"lets see... <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Uktena of the Waterway</b></span><br /> Uktena of the Waterway is a wise old spirit, and has seen many things in its long existence. It has always been willing to use its power and influence on behalf of those who make the appropriate offerings and sacrifices. But something has changed- the spirit has grown violent and capricious, and rumors of it preying upon the local mortals have begun to circulate. Uktena of the Waterway takes the form of an enormous serpent, with scales that shine like crystal and head crowned with the horns of a stag. A large gemstone is affixed in its brow, which glows with a blinding light.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Rivers 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Will not attack a person carrying water from the Hidden Spring (unless attacked first); <b>Bane:</b> an arrow,wrapped in the skin of venomous snake, driven through its heart<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Shadow Gateway, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Blast (Poison Breath), Implant Mission, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Strike Blind, Twilight Abduction</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Strike Blind: </b>The entity using this Numen may blind people over an area, whether using darkness or blinding light (chosen when gained and appropriate to the entity in question). Activating the Numen requires 1 Essence and affects an area with a radius of the entity\u2019s Power in yards, causing the Blinded Tilt. Characters may resist with Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance. The effect is magical in origin but can be dealt with in mundane fashion, such as by activating light sources to partially negate darkness or a welder\u2019s mask to help reduce blinding glare. The Tilt lasts until the entity dismisses it, leaves the area, or the scene ends.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Twilight Abduction: </b>The entity can attempt to drag victims within one yard into an incorporeal state, allowing it to freely interact with the target. Spend three Essence points, and roll the entities\u2019 (Power + Finesse) .The target resists with a roll of (Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance). If the entity wins, shadows drag the victim and his worn possessions through a sudden imploding tear in space. In an instant, the rift closes, and the victim enters Twilight for one hour per remaining success.</span> <hr /><br /> As for a plot element, the first idea that comes to mind is that the Hidden Spring is the source of the Spirits power, and the conduit that feeds its essence.The rites of the Pure have poisoned its essence, making the spirit cruel and violent. In order to be healed, the resonance of the spring must be purified and restored to its original state, which is likely easier said than done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T15:44:04-07:00","id":896357,"title":"","content":"Buh-rilliant! Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:34:23-07:00","id":897197,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a list of special boons that some spirit may grant to those who offers them the right offering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-25T09:42:19-07:00","id":899029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com