07:00","id":902262,"title":"","content":"A few new spirits I have cooked up ...<br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Asphalt Serpent</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirit called \u201cAsphalt Serpent\u201d is a road spirit, who maintains and protects a stretch of winding road approximately 2 miles long. It plagues those who do not pay the proper respect with mechanical failure and other mishaps. The spirit appears as a large black serpentine creature with asphalt for scales and is patterned with road markings. Its eyes flash green, yellow and red.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 4, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Roads 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest on a Roadway; <b>Bane: </b>Soil from beneath a paved crossroad<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Innocuous, Left-Handed Spanner, Pathfinder, Stalwart</span><br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Covetous Stampede</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cCovetous Stampede\u201d is a spirit of greed who gains essence from the desperate need to obtain popular items. The type of item does not matter; it could be a toy, and athletic sneaker, or the latest smartphone model. As long as people are willing to harm themselves or others to gain the item, Covetous Stampede grows strong. Covetous Stampede appears as a muscular, androgynous creature with the hooves of a bull. Its flesh is patterned with icons and logos of the latest fads, with the symbols older fads fading as they fall out of fashion.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Greed 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest near a recent fad item; <b>Bane: </b>The crushed remains of a recent fad item<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Drain, Rapture, Seek, Sign</span><br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Last Merciful Breath</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cLast Merciful Breath\u201d is a spirit of death and mercy. It draws its essence from the final moments of a dying person\u2019s life. It is not a cruel spirit, and uses it power to ease the suffering of the dying. It is powerful, and knows many secrets from long years of traveling the depths of the Underworld. The spirit appears as a skeletal woman wearing a dark veil and a laurel of withered flowers.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 9, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Death 2, Mercy 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest near a dying person; <b>Bane: </b>the ashes of a person tortured to death<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Realm Gateway (Underworld)*, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Essence Thief, Omen Trance, Seek, Speed</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Manifestation \u2013 Realm Gateway:</b> The World of Darkness holds many spiritual realms. Some non-native entities have managed to find ways to enter these realms, exploring them for their own reasons. To do so, the entity must find an appropriate point of ingress, such as a locus, Avernian gate, or dormant gate to the Hedge and spend 2Essence. Each time this power is selected, it is keyed to a specific non-native realm. It may be picked multiple times, once for each realm the entity would like to access.</span><br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Merchant of Lost Dreams</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cThe Merchant of Lost Dreams\u201d is a spirit of the Pawn Shop, and draws its essence when a person trades a long term desire or precious memento for an immediate need. It has gained great insight into human nature and does not hesitate to use that knowledge for its own gain. The spirit is a dark, slim creature with six long, spindly arms, vaguely human features, and a wide, ever- present grin filled with yellow teeth.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Desire 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can never go back on a Deal; <b>Bane: </b>Pyrite/Fool\u2019s Gold<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Drain, Mixed Blessing (Resources 2)*, Telekinesis, Transmute*</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina - Mixed Blessing: </b>The entity can bestow a number of dots equal to the entities rank in a specific merit to a mortal. The Merit is chosen when this Numina is selected and cannot be changed at a later time, but may be split between multiple merits. This Numen costs Essence equal to the dots in the bestowed Merit and last s for one day per activation success. For the duration of the Numen\u2019s effect, the mortal gains the Leveraged Condition in relation to the bestowing entity. At any time, the mortal can buy the Merit at half cost, rounded down. This makes the Condition Persistent. The Persistent Condition can then only be resolved if the entity chooses to release the mortal, or is destroyed. This Numen may be selected multiple times, each one representing a different Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Transmute: </b>Some spirits and angels possess the ability to transform one type of matter into another. More precious materials and those with mystical significance require greater effort to transmute. The Numen requires a Finesse + Resistance roll to activate. Transmuting common materials such as grave dirt or dead wood into other common materials costs 1 Essence. Creating valuable materials like gold or gemstones requires 3 Essence, and the roll suffers a \u20132 penalty. Transmuting objects into matter with mystical significance like silver or alchemical substances requires 5 Essence and suffers a \u20134 penalty. This Numen may not be used on living things.</span> <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:16:04-07:00","id":904574,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Hunter in Moon Shadows </b></span><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3 (Spirit)<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 6, Finesse 6, Resistance 4,<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 17<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>8<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Hunting 2, Darkness 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must engage in a successful hunt every month or lose all Willpower<br /> <b>Bane: </b>A sliver blown from a lightning-blasted tree.<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Reaching, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Speed<br /> <b>Description:</b> A cougar stepping out of the shadows into a shaft of moonlight. It is exquisite, the perfect predator; you can sense the silent power in each silent step. It looks out at you, calculating, and then melts into the darkness again, briefly... to give you a chance to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","user":"Corrigan","date":".  Raised Attributes 06-01-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:27:26-07:00","id":904613,"title":"","content":"Kinda low attributes for a rank 3 spirit, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:30:46-07:00","id":904915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=904613#post904613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda low attributes for a rank 3 spirit, I believe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you're right. The rank got bumped up halfway through the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:19:34-07:00","id":906864,"title":"","content":"A few more spirits for the weekend <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fanatic Paramour </b></span><br /> The entity called \u201cFanatic Paramour\u201d is a spirit of infatuation taken to unhealthy extremes. The spirit uses its influence to fan idle crushes and passing romantic musings into violent obsessions and feeds on the essence of such acts. It appears as an apparition composed primarily of red vapor; with six dark, sinuous arms and a floating white mask with weeping eyes drawn on the surface.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 7, Finesse 4, Resistance 3, Willpower 7 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 11, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Infatuation 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use influence or numina on a person in a happy romantic relationship <b>Bane: </b>ashes from burned love letters<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>One Thousand Treacherous Tongues</b></span><br /> \u201cOne Thousand Treacherous Tongues\u201d is a spirit of malicious lies and slander. It gains its essence from those who lie to cause another pain or discomfort, and uses its power to encourage such behavior. It appears as a vaguely female form, with a face, chest, abdomen, and genitals on both the front and back of its body and double-jointed limbs. In both its mouths are multiple lolling tongues, each one over a foot long and jet black. Despite this, the entity speaks clearly and eloquently.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 9, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Lies 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can never utter a truth, will discorporate if forced <b>Bane: </b>White Chrysanthemum <br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Dement, Hallucination, Seek, Sign, Speed</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Promise of Dust</b></span><br /> The Promise of Dust is a spirit of Drought, and it gains its essence when the land is parched from long periods of little or no rainfall. It uses its power and influence to extend the drought, causing water supplies to evaporate and chasing away rainclouds. When manifested. Promise of Dust is a tall figure with grey, desiccated flesh, wearing a rough spun robe and coated in a fine layer of powdered earth. A stifling heat radiates from its form.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 12, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 18, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 12, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Drought 4, Heat 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest where has not rained in over 30 days; <b>Bane: </b>Natural Rain<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (Desiccation), Drain, Firestarter, Seek, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Scrapyard Mongrel</b></span><br /> Scrapyard Mongrel is a spirit that resides in the scrap yard, it domain the twisting mazes of ruined vehicles and rusted metal. It is a territorial creature, and will attack anyone that enters its territory without the proper appeasement. The spirit is a large canid- seeming amalgam of auto parts and rusted steel, all wrapped in barbed wire and dripping dark oil. Its eyes glow as bright as headlights.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 3, Resistance 5, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 18<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Metal 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest outside of the scrapyard <b>Bane: </b>wood wrapped in leather<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (metal shards), Left \u2013 Handed Spanner, Nightmare Weaponry*, Speed, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Nightmare Weaponry: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest claws, fangs, horns, suckers, or other appropriate natural weaponry. The modification acts as a 1L weapon</span>.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:30:28-07:00","id":912213,"title":"","content":"this weeks set <hr /><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Crashing Hand of the Tide</span> </b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Crashing Hand of the Tide is a spirit of the pounding surf, and is ancient, powerful, and inscrutable. It is endlessly persistent, and once it has decided on a course of action it cannot stop until the task is done. It manifests has a massive luminescent wave of water, shapes can be observed moving within its rippling depths.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 5[Spirit]<br /> Power 13, Finesse 10, Resistance 15, Willpower 10, Essence 50<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 35, <b>Size</b> 20, <b>Initiative</b> 25, <b>Defense</b> 15, <b>Speed</b> 38<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Waves 5, Persistence 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Once it starts a task, it cannot stop until the task is completed; <b>Bane:</b> granite - heated to a burning temperature<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Wave of Water), Drain, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Molten Stone Fire</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cMolten Stone Fire\u201d is a nature spirit of lava, and dwells in places where volcanic activity impacts human settlement. The spirit is confident, and determined, and takes great delight in burning obstacles into ash. It appears as a child with skin made of cracked black stone with radiant fire appearing within the cracks. Its hair is a wild halo of flames.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Lava 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b> Cannot manifest more than a day\u2019s walk from an active lava flow <b>Bane: </b>Sea Water<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Bane Sense*, Blast (Lava), Firestarter, Pathfinder, Regenerate</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina - Bane Sense: </b>An ephemeral entity is largely immune to harm except from specific sources. One of those sources is its Bane, and its senses are attuned to detecting danger. It gains the Danger Sense (Advanced) Merit in relation to its Bane.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Shelter of Leaves</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cShelter of Leaves\u201d dwells within a large oak tree that sits in a glade far from the beaten path in a national forest. It has been visited by campers and hikers willing to make the trip for decades. It is a spirit of protection, shielding those within its glade from sun and storm. Shelter of Leaves manifests as a spry old man made of rugged wood, with a beard of leaves and wearing a crown of twigs and acorns. <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 4, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 25, <b>Size</b> 16, <b>Initiative</b> 13, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 12<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Trees 2, Protection 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must slumber during Winter <b>Bane: </b>An axe with no wooden elements<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Image, Gauntlet Breach, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Heal*, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Regenerate, Stalwart</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina - Heal: </b>The entity can heal others\u2019 wounds, typically for a hefty price. This Numen costs 1 Essence and a Power+ Finesse roll to activate. Each success heals a level of bashing damage, while two successes can heal a point of lethal damage. The lethal damage healed can be used to mend aggravated damage, but each point of aggravated damage cured costs three additional points of Essence. This power may also be used to fight off disease or the effects of poison \u2014 each success adding to the subjects\u2019 resistance rolls on a one-to-one basis.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T15:54:37-07:00","id":913048,"title":"","content":"Hello, I was wondering if someone could help me out. I have a game I am running of Requiem set in 1191 AD. The characters are going to be entering in to the city of Bishops Lin where currently there is a feud between the Blood Talons who are of Norwegian descent and still hold the Nordic faith in high esteem and the Iron Masters most of whom are influencing the Christian church. Now I was wondering if I could get help because both would need totems that correspond with their religions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:40:19-07:00","id":916154,"title":"","content":"<b>Knowledge base Spirit</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Knowledge base is a spirit from </span>technology <span style=\"font-size:12px\">court. His </span>rank can vary depending on how much time the material datarcenter/KnowledgeBase has grown.<br /> They reside in cold and dark chambers because they can better influence in these locations. <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Very weak knowledge base spirits appears as an </span>transparent monitor, when it moves the monitor almost disappearer getting extremely ephemeral. When he stops at a fixed location he sticks his cables on the ground and it gets more material.<br /> These spirits have the all the information of the enterprise they are attached to it. <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Knowledge stored on computers 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must acquire new information<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Remains of destroyed Server or Harddrive.<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Innocuous, Omen Trance, Telekinesis, Telepathy<br /> <br /> Stronger KnowledgeBase spirits can be more<a href=\"http://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/t_original/hyo64qiomsb455sp1ixm.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> alien and wierd</a> and way harder to get information.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T06:43:37-07:00","id":916158,"title":"","content":"Any ideas for rank 1 spirits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:55:26-07:00","id":916199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=916158#post916158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas for rank 1 spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they are barely sentient/animalistic, so there isn't much distinction between them. General ideas: Garbage Collection spirits, Coffee spirits, Spark spirits. Just thing that loiter around their reflections, drinking up Essence. Mostly serve as scenery for food for greater Spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:22:49-07:00","id":916225,"title":"","content":"<b>Rotworm</b><br /> Reflections of basic concepts of decay, including decomposers, rotworms appear as lethargic green worms with pale white veins, a contracting sphincter acting as a mouth at the 'front.' One can easily see how close they are to becoming hursah, as those nearing the next rank bulge as if over-stuffed and act more energetically. Opportunistic and swarming predators, in the rare occasions they find themselves in the gurihal rotworms often fetter themselves to trash or, preferably, the dead.<br /> <b>Rank</b>: 1<br /> <b>Power </b>2, <b>Finesse </b>1, <b>Resistance </b>2, <b>Willpower </b>3, <b>Essence </b>10<br /> <b>Corpus </b>3, <b>Size </b>1, <b>Initiative </b>3, <b>Defense </b>2, <b>Speed </b>4<br /> <b>Influence</b>: Decay<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Rotworms must move towards any dead or decaying material nearby, not including the supernaturally preserved dead, like vampires <b>Bane</b>: Fire<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Fetter<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Entropic Decay, Innocuous<br /> <br /> <b>Graveworm</b><br /> Thicker and longer than their hursih predecessors they're often found surrounded by, graveworms are more like snakes, ranging from one to five feet long and as thick around as a human's leg. They tend to look green or brown or black, and are surrounded by a musty stench of rotting flesh. More firmly bound to death, they usually inhabit graveyards or the dens of killers, but will occasionally be seen in the wilderness or near it, feasting on roadkill and other dead animals. In the rare occasions they can, they are known to use their powers through the Gauntlet to turn the dying into the dead.<br /> <b>Rank</b>: 2<br /> <b>Power </b>4, <b>Finesse </b>2, <b>Resistance </b>3, <b>Willpower </b>5, <b>Essence </b>15<br /> <b>Corpus </b>6, <b>Size </b>3, <b>Initiative</b> 5, <b>Defense </b>2, <b>Speed </b>9<br /> <b>Influence</b>: Decay 1, Death 1<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Bleeds 1 Essence every hour it's not near something Dead-Resonant as if it was in the guriahl <b>Bane</b>: Any object that has been sterilized<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Fetter, Reaching<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Dement, Drain, Entropic Decay, Innocuous, Seek<br /> <br /> Having a hard time figuring out appropriate bans for the ranks. I figure the Graveworm would be a specific kind of 'evolution' from the rotworm, one that has been around dead humans and animals, rather than garbage and other organics, which might become Rustworms or Moldworms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:07:07-07:00","id":918395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=913048#post913048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I was wondering if someone could help me out. I have a game I am running of Requiem set in 1191 AD. The characters are going to be entering in to the city of Bishops Lin where currently there is a feud between the Blood Talons who are of Norwegian descent and still hold the Nordic faith in high esteem and the Iron Masters most of whom are influencing the Christian church. Now I was wondering if I could get help because both would need totems that correspond with their religions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kept meaning to reply to this, mainly because I love me Medieval Christianity and Norse culture. Hope it isn't too late for your game!<br /> <br /> Firstly, I'd say that you shouldn't feel enslaved to the religions for totem ideas. It's not like every American has Jesus as a totem, eh? I've mined some religious ideas below, but also some cultural and regional touchstones (heh), as well. If there are any you're interested in, I can help stat 'em up if you like (or someone else can; we've got some geniuses in this thread!)<br /> <br /> <b>Wall's-Blessed-Strength</b><br /> A spirit of stone and protection, or perhaps the spirit of the walls encircling a Christian settlement. It appears as a robed warrior with a battered old sword, chiselled entirely out of stone, with eyes of eternal flames. On the rare times it speaks, its voice booms like a mighty drawbridge heaving into place. Every movement sounds like great stones scraping against one another. While the spirit's might is famous across Norway, it's also its greatest weakness - Wall's-Blessed-Strength can not refuse protection to a Christian traveller, and should the flame at the top of its highest tower ever go out, it will fall into Slumber.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Goat That Howls At Night</b> (Never said the Iron Masters had to be good Christians, right?)<br /> This spirit is old, and has walked the land for many years. When the invaders came - casting down the old gods, mocking them, literally demonising them - most of the spirits hated them. Not the Black Goat. Nourished on Christian folklore, it grew from a simple goat spirit into a symbol of everything they fear. The pack that serve it hide among the herd, but - like their totem - must embrace the townsfolk's superstitions, risking discovery at every turn. Every Sunday, though, it flees into the wilds, for it cannot abide the sound of church bells.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye-Biter</b><br /> A spirit of hidden knowledge, appearing as a flock of ravens that speak as one. Like Odin's messengers, it will whisper many things of past and future to its pack, but always at a cost - it cannot communicate without hurting the listener. Its pack suffers a weaker version of its Ban - they must cause pain, either physical or metaphorical, when they tell a secret. Even so, they're eager to live up to their totem's style; their tongues are wicked barbs, and they foment trouble wherever they go. Whenever they speak, trouble is sure to arise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":2653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","user":"NateD","date":". 06-20-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T22:34:55-07:00","id":918448,"title":"","content":"Oooh, more ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>Ravaging Flame</b><br /> For decades, this spirit of fiery destruction went a'viking far and wide with a pack of Blood Talons - now, however, it aids them in driving the Christian invaders from their homeland. Its Ban is simple, and one that its pack is only too eager to uphold - each week it must completely destroy something of value by flame or fall to Slumber. Its Bane, however, is more problematic - it cannot abide a human dwelling made completely of stone. It avoids stone buildings altogether; somehow being forced to step onto the floor of one is certain death.<br /> <br /> <b>The-Walker-on-the-Road</b><br /> This spirit ceaselessly travels the old Roman Roads of Scandinavia, its two faces partially obscured beneath the hood of a camel-hair monk's robe. Though it never speaks, it will reveal many secrets of the Hisil to its pack. While many others believe the Walker is a spirit of pilgrims and the monastic life, its pack knows it is much older than the Christian holy men that now travel its byways. According to them, it is a spirit of the supernatural itself - the walker-between that treads the road between the gods and flesh. Others might balk at this, if the pack ever spoke of it to outsiders - but they won't. Sworn to permanent silence, the pack's alpha even cut her own tongue from her mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:13:28-07:00","id":920131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NateD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=918395#post918395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kept meaning to reply to this, mainly because I love me Medieval Christianity and Norse culture. Hope it isn't too late for your game!<br /> Firstly, I'd say that you shouldn't feel enslaved to the religions for totem ideas. It's not like every American has Jesus as a totem, eh? I've mined some religious ideas below, but also some cultural and regional touchstones (heh), as well. If there are any you're interested in, I can help stat 'em up if you like (or someone else can; we've got some geniuses in this thread!)<br /> <br /> <b>Wall's-Blessed-Strength</b><br /> A spirit of stone and protection, or perhaps the spirit of the walls encircling a Christian settlement. It appears as a robed warrior with a battered old sword, chiselled entirely out of stone, with eyes of eternal flames. On the rare times it speaks, its voice booms like a mighty drawbridge heaving into place. Every movement sounds like great stones scraping against one another. While the spirit's might is famous across Norway, it's also its greatest weakness - Wall's-Blessed-Strength can not refuse protection to a Christian traveller, and should the flame at the top of its highest tower ever go out, it will fall into Slumber.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Goat That Howls At Night</b> (Never said the Iron Masters had to be good Christians, right?)<br /> This spirit is old, and has walked the land for many years. When the invaders came - casting down the old gods, mocking them, literally demonising them - most of the spirits hated them. Not the Black Goat. Nourished on Christian folklore, it grew from a simple goat spirit into a symbol of everything they fear. The pack that serve it hide among the herd, but - like their totem - must embrace the townsfolk's superstitions, risking discovery at every turn. Every Sunday, though, it flees into the wilds, for it cannot abide the sound of church bells.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye-Biter</b><br /> A spirit of hidden knowledge, appearing as a flock of ravens that speak as one. Like Odin's messengers, it will whisper many things of past and future to its pack, but always at a cost - it cannot communicate without hurting the listener. Its pack suffers a weaker version of its Ban - they must cause pain, either physical or metaphorical, when they tell a secret. Even so, they're eager to live up to their totem's style; their tongues are wicked barbs, and they foment trouble wherever they go. Whenever they speak, trouble is sure to arise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for these and no it is not too late. I have had to postpone the game for a few weeks until I finished my exams and I have just enough time to finish the packs in my game. I really like these spirits so thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T17:23:21-07:00","id":921768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Anubi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=920131#post920131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you so much for these and no it is not too late. I have had to postpone the game for a few weeks until I finished my exams and I have just enough time to finish the packs in my game. I really like these spirits so thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, and glad you like 'em. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:11:59-07:00","id":935487,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The totem I created for a neolithic crossover game I'm in. My Uratha, my wolfblood and an NPC are the contributors. We use the optional Fate system from the Chronicles of Darkness (pg 177) and it\u2019s sort of built with that in mind. The totem was formerly the Wolfblooded familiar of my Uratha, tied to her at birth (perhaps due to her Fate, \u2018Martyred\u2019).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Last Whisper</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Last Whisper appears as a large pale-eyed bird whose feathers fall to the floor as he flies, vanishing in tiny puffs of black smoke as they touch the earth. It appears as a large crow or vulture, depending on which of it\u2019s influences (or numina) it has most recently indulged in. If it has indulged in neither influence for more than a week, it appears instead as a hawk as it searches for resonant essence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Rank 2</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Blessing: </b>Cursed, Striking Looks: Unsettling (or Striking Looks: Touched by Death to those with knowledge of the Supernatural) - Expression, Intimidation</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Influences:</b> Omens: 1 (Crow), Death: 1 (Vulture)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Numina: </b>Omen Trance (Crow), Ghost Eater (Vulture), Seek (Hawk)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Power:</b> 3, Finesse 4, Resistance 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Aspiration</b>: To hear a person\u2019s dying words.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Ban:</b> Must never interrupt, contradict or interfere with an omen</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Bane: </b>A strike from anyone who has met their Fate and survived</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Corpus: 5, Willpower: 6</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Size: 2, Defense: 3, Speed 17 (Species Factor 10 as per a Raven), Initiative: 7</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-22-2016, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T03:22:20-07:00","id":935497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/856576-sample-spirits?p=935487#post935487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The totem I created for a neolithic crossover game I'm in. My Uratha, my wolfblood and an NPC are the contributors. We use the optional Fate system from the Chronicles of Darkness (pg 177) and it\u2019s sort of built with that in mind. The totem was formerly the Wolfblooded familiar of my Uratha, tied to her at birth (perhaps due to her Fate, \u2018Martyred\u2019).</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting spirit you got there. Also, I can't seem to find the text concerning that system on my copy of the book. All I found instead was a tidbit related to the God-Machine. Care to PM it to me, if it's alright?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/ma